  "description": "<p>When committing a long running Fedora transaction, in which the time needed to perform the commit is long (due to a large total size of files of many gigabytes and a large numbers of files for example), the database connections needs to stay open for a long time without any activity because moving all those files from OCFL staging directory to the OCFL root (committing the OCFL persistent storage session, <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/a2ec2ac5b273670c421b74df1ad9174b3289f663/fcrepo-kernel-impl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/impl/TransactionImpl.java#L361\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">fcrepo-kernel-impl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/impl/TransactionImpl.java#L361</a>) can take a considerable amount of time.</p>\n\n<p>The current implementation makes it hard to commit larger Fedora transactions that create/update many Fedora ressources and/or add large binary contents.</p>\n\n<p>Extract of the log message when committing the dabase transcaction because it has been closed by the database server or because the underlying TCP connection has been closed: </p>\n\n<p><span class=\"nobr\"><a href=\"/rest/api/3/attachment/content/10417\" title=\"fedora_db_connection_timeout_stack_trace.txt attached to FCREPO-3970\" data-attachment-type=\"file\" data-attachment-name=\"fedora_db_connection_timeout_stack_trace.txt\" data-media-services-type=\"file\" data-media-services-id=\"00c852bd-02f1-48ec-8c60-45cd655e3345\" rel=\"noreferrer\">fedora_db_connection_timeout_stack_trace.txt<sup><img class=\"rendericon\" src=\"/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif\" height=\"7\" width=\"7\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"/></sup></a></span> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>If connection drops are frequent it can be problematic to keep the database connections alive by adjusting the parameters (different security zone, network hardware that is configured to kill long connection…).  </p>\n\n<p>Especially in environments of our customers it’s hard to finetune/adjust all parts involved in this (e.g. Firewall, settings of a central PostgreSQL database).</p>\n\n\n\n<p>It would greatly improve the situation if moving the files from OCFL staging to the OCFL root could be done before opening or after committing the database transaction.</p>",
  "duedate": null,
  "environment": "Our cloud setup:<br/>\n<br/>\nFedora<br/>\n- Version: 6.5.0<br/>\n- keepaliveTime=30sec<br/>\n<br/>\nPostgres:<br/>\n- Version: 12.16<br/>\n- Custom settings: idle_in_transaction_session_timeout=180 minutes<br/>\n<br/>\nDeployed as a docker stack. The database container is in endpoint_mode: dnsrr and the port is in mode: host<br/>\n<br/>\nOur customers environments can differ and our mostly running on Windows servers.",
